WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:07.530
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and because last
week we got a big white walker surprise I

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:13.030
wanted to do a bonus video that talked about
the last great war with them and the building

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.030
of The Wall.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.340
One of the really cool things about the show
and the books are that you learn a lot about

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.180
history anecdotally.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:25.130
That is characters themselves reading things
in books and making casual references.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.770
So that’s where most of our info on the
White Walkers and the Great Other come from.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.590
If you’re finding me for the first time
each week I’m doing special bonus videos

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.230
just to celebrate season 4.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.982
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
leave me suggestions for topics you’d like

00:00:37.982 --> 00:00:38.982
to see.

00:00:38.982 --> 00:00:41.930
My episode 5 video will post tonight after
the episode airs.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:52.571
So the funny thing about most of the characters
on the show is that like Jon Snow, they know

00:00:52.571 --> 00:00:54.600
nothing of the Long Night.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.690
Remember when Old Nan made that “Sweet Summer
Child” speech in season 1?

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:02.120
She was talking to the Stark children because
they had been born during the Long Summer.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.389
The world of Game of Thrones is weird in that
seasons last for indeterminate amounts of

00:01:06.389 --> 00:01:07.389
time.

00:01:07.389 --> 00:01:11.229
So the summer as of season 1 had lasted for
10 years.

00:01:11.229 --> 00:01:17.979
Right now, right after the purple wedding
is officially the beginning of Winter.

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:21.770
Winter has come.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:26.659
I think that’s one of the reasons Dan and
Dave chose to include that White Walker scene

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:32.689
in episode 4.

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:38.289
The Long Night was a little bit different
in that it was a period of extreme darkness

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:39.880
that lasted for a generation.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.079
So it was more than just a Long Winter.

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:46.369
When they say Generation I think we can assume
based on life expectancy that it was about

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:47.369
50 or 60 years.

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:51.429
Old Nan was the first person to mention the
Long Night in season 1.

00:01:51.429 --> 00:01:56.849
She was trying to tell Bran the story of Brandon
the Builder.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.029
His Stark Ancestor that built the Wall at
the end of the Long Night.

00:02:00.029 --> 00:02:02.109
That period in history was during the time
of the First Men.

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:05.919
Remember in Season 2 they visited the Fist
of the First Men.

00:02:05.919 --> 00:02:09.140
That’s when Jon Snow’s story split off
with Ygritte and Sam saw the White Walker

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.140
for the first time.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:19.700
There was a 
person called The Last Hero and when you look

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.110
at his triumph over the white walkers he sounds
a lot like Melisandre’s version of Azor

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.860
Ahai, just someone who saves the world from
darkness.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.800
There’s some books about him at the Night’s
Watch that talk about the Obsidian blades

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.630
being able to hurt them.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.650
We really only learn about this more as Sam
learns about it.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.360
So I’m hoping we get to see more of him
in the library.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:44.680
One of the big problems with all the books
everyone has are that none of them were written

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.860
while the Long Night was happening.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:50.350
Everything was written my Maesters and scholars
thousands of years later.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.600
In the chronology of the show.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.580
The Long Night was actually about 8,000 years
ago.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.800
The Children of the Forest were a big part
of this time in history.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.150
Technically it’s referred to as the Age
of Heroes.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.960
It began when the first men signed a pact
with the Children to end a different war and

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.580
it’s believed that the Last Hero, when he
ended the Long Night, did so with the help

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.600
of the Children.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.360
Again, we only learn about these types of
things when characters on the show tell it

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.740
to other characters.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:26.450
I’m hoping that George RR Martin’s upcoming
books go into much greater detail.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.620
Here’s where we need to talk about The Wall
and Brandon the Builder.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.540
He was the founder of House Stark.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.710
We know he was alive at the end of the Long
Night, but I can’t confirm he was present

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:39.130
at the signing of the Pact between the Children
of The Forest and the First Men.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.730
There’s no official timeline for those events.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:42.730
Yet.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:47.950
The rumors say that when Brandon built the
wall he had help from the Giants and probably

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.120
wildlings too.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:53.800
After a war like the Long Night you can imagine
most people put their differences aside.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:58.000
So anyone who was not a servant of the Great
Other probably helped build it.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.600
There are supposed magic runes and wards that
protect it, but we haven’t learned anything

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.600
official about that yet.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.440
When it was first built they used a lot of
the natural mountains in the area to provide

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:07.440
the foundation.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.140
So it’s not like they were building a 300
mile long 700 foot high block of ice on completely

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.140
flat ground.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.270
It’s just that because the Wall sits on
top of mountains at certain points, you can’t

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.270
see them.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.739
Supposedly the big blocks of ice they used
were quarried from the lakes in the haunted

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:21.609
forest and the Wall just slowly got bigger
over the centuries.

00:04:21.609 --> 00:04:24.580
Meaning that when it was first built, during
Brandon lifetime.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.020
It was way smaller.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.060
I think that’s way more plausible.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.133
And the members of the Night’s Watch just
slowly added to it over time until it got

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.650
to the size it is right now.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:37.690
For example, the Great Wall of China was built
over a period of Two Thousand Years.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:42.509
They did not have Giants helping, so maybe
shave off a couple hundred years for Brandon’s

00:04:42.509 --> 00:04:43.509
Wall.

00:04:43.509 --> 00:04:47.400
When it first started the Night’s Watch
had an army of men helping out.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:53.930
At it’s biggest there were about 10,000
men serving in 19 castles along The Wall.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.849
Right now there are only three castles being
used and a handful of men manning them.

00:04:56.849 --> 00:05:00.740
They’re using the Shadow Tower, Castle Black
and Eastwatch.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:05.180
They’re basically three castles that are
equidistant from each other from the westernmost

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.389
part of The Wall to the Easternmost part.

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:12.810
With Castle Black being in the middle.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.789
During Season 2 Mance Rayder talked about
destroying The Wall with something called

00:05:15.789 --> 00:05:18.070
the Horn of Winter.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:27.360
It’s a legendary horn that belonged to Joramun
the Wildling King that helped defeat the Night’s

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.550
King.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.020
The horn was used to call the Giants to him.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:35.090
But it’s also supposed to be able to bring
The Wall down.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:38.400
We don’t know if this is true, but ‘bringing
the wall down’ could be a literal interpretation

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.180
of Giants just smashing it physically.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:46.470
The Horn that Mance Rayder claims is the Horn
of Winter is about eight feet long with Runes

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:47.889
of The First Men on it.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:51.770
The thing I really like about the show and
the books are that because most of this information

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:53.930
is passed along in the form of legend.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.599
There’s no way to know what’s true and
what’s been fabricated.

00:05:57.599 --> 00:06:01.659
We know Dragons exist and we know that magic
exists.

00:06:01.659 --> 00:06:05.400
We just saw that the White Walkers have a
very real culture and home of their own.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.409
That’s supposedly located up in the Lands
of Always Winter.

00:06:08.409 --> 00:06:11.741
You can see it here on a map just to give
you an idea of how far away it is from the

00:06:11.741 --> 00:06:13.880
rest of Westeros and The Wall.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:17.969
As you can see based on the distance from
The Wall to Winterfell, the supposed home

00:06:17.969 --> 00:06:19.699
of the White Walkers isn’t that far away.

00:06:19.699 --> 00:06:28.740
But they are separated by this great mountain
range.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:34.089
We don’t know how big their army is right
now, but in my last video I speculated that

00:06:34.089 --> 00:06:38.210
because Craster had sacrificed all 99 of his
sons, there were at least 100 White Walkers

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.949
including the Night’s King.

00:06:39.949 --> 00:06:43.670
They raise wights to form their infantry,
but we don’t know if every White Walker

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.309
possesses the same magic as the Night’s
King.

00:06:46.309 --> 00:06:48.439
I would assume yes.

00:06:48.439 --> 00:06:53.949
I think of them as being like Melisandre and
Thoros, who each have the same powers, even

00:06:53.949 --> 00:06:56.529
though each acolyte has their own specialties.

00:06:56.529 --> 00:07:01.490
Melisandre can conjure visions and birth shadow
babies and Thoros can bring people back to

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:02.490
life.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.340
I would assume the White Walkers each have
their own specialties too.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:11.289
I don’t think we’ll learn more about that
until we get more books, so let me know what

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:15.800
other things you’re most hoping to learn
about them.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.120
Either on the show or in the books.

